=== HOW THIS COMPANY INTERVIEWS (use this to calibrate) ===
- Rounds mix three things: (1) DSA at easy-to-medium level (arrays, strings, hashing, stacks, linked lists, trees, BFS/DFS on grids and graphs, basic DP, intervals, binary search); (2) core CS fundamentals with a strong lean toward operating systems, computer networks, DBMS/SQL and OOP; (3) a deep dive into the candidate’s own projects, sometimes with a managerial flavour (“how would you handle…”).
- Interviewers value thought process, clear communication and fundamentals over a perfect first answer. They prefer real-life examples and scenarios over textbook definitions.
